label s34
text @[Tomoya]
text About the old man.
sound R0O.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text You're thinking about Dad?
text @[Tomoya]
text Yeah...
text @[Tomoya]
text I always felt like... he just went around doing whatever he wanted...
text @[Tomoya]
text but I finally kind of realized, he doesn't do that just for himself.
sound R0P.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text Who does he do it for, then?
text @[Tomoya]
text No, well, probably not for anyone in particular...
text @[Tomoya]
text and he himself is probably still just doing whatever it is he wants to do...
text @[Tomoya]
text but despite all that, a lot of people need him.
music BGM08D.mp3
text I wonder if I've been acting similarly.
text Could I have helped out those kids that were aiming to become regulars in their baseball team?
text Help them out with their fielding practice?
text I might, if the kids actually enjoyed it.
text In that case, I wonder if I could even find myself wanting to go fix people's bath heaters without them even asking me.
text Could I do that, just to kill off some time?
text No, not me, at least.
sound R0Q.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text Dad just wants to see everyone smile.
sound R0R.aac
text @[Nagisa]
text I'm sure that's all there is to it.
text I'd felt this too, whenever I stood next to him.
text Watching him, as he made others smile.
text Yeah... it kind of gets on my nerves.
text Still...
text It makes me wonder just how anxious Sanae-san must feel all the time.
text Since at any time...
text That guy can just go off somewhere to make someone smile. That's the kind of husband she's burdened with.
